&lt;p&gt;Toast creates technology to help restaurants and local businesses succeed in a digital world, helping business owners operate, increase sales, engage customers, and keep employees happy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring the first Bookkeepers on our Financial Management team — a founding, hands-on role at the intersection of real client bookkeeping and 0-to-1 product building. You won&#39;t be joining an established practice with a mature playbook; you&#39;ll be writing it. You&#39;ll do the actual books for our earliest restaurant customers while working shoulder-to-shoulder with product and engineering to shape the service, tooling, and workflows that will define how Toast delivers bookkeeping at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for someone who genuinely likes restaurant bookkeeping — the prime cost, the tip reporting, the multi-location chaos — and who also gets energy from questioning industry norms and building something new rather than maintaining something established.&amp;nbsp; Ambiguity here isn&#39;t a bug; for the first year or two, it&#39;s the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re the kind of person who reads a messy set of restaurant books and sees an interesting puzzle — and who&#39;d rather build the recipe than follow one — we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Location Requirement: &lt;/strong&gt;This position requires 2 days per week on-site at our Boston office (located in the Seaport).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life (Responsibilities)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end bookkeeping for a portfolio of pilot restaurant customers: chart of accounts setup, monthly close, bank/POS reconciliations, accruals, and delivery of clean financial statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as Toast&#39;s in-house expert on restaurant-specific accounting — prime cost, COGS, labor and tip reporting, multi-unit consolidation, high-volume daily transaction reconciliation, and multi-jurisdiction sales tax.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed directly with product and engineering, translating real client workflows and pain points into product requirements that shape our roadmap — you&#39;ll be in the room when we decide what to build next, not just told what shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and document the SOPs, controls, and QA processes a bookkeeping function needs to run reliably — since none of it exists yet, you&#39;ll build the foundation others will scale on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with restaurant operators to understand their businesses, set expectations, and deliver a service that earns their trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define what “great” looks like for this function as it grows, including future hiring needs, tooling choices, and where automation should (and shouldn&#39;t) replace judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move fluidly between hands-on bookkeeping work and higher-leverage building work as priorities shift — comfort wearing both hats is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need to thrive (Requirements)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+years of bookkeeping experience, with meaningful time spent on restaurant or hospitality clients specifically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of restaurant accounting mechanics: COGS and prime cost, tip pooling and reporting, multi-location consolidation, and reconciling high-volume POS transaction data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with modern bookkeeping and accounting software, and genuine enthusiasm for adopting new tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a process or practice from scratch.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine comfort with ambiguity and undefined scope; you&#39;d rather help define a role than be handed a finished one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills — able to translate accounting complexity into plain language for both restaurant operators and internal product/engineering partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sharp attention to detail and the organizational discipline to manage multiple clients&#39; books accurately and on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will help you stand out (Nonessential Skills/Nice to Haves)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a tech startup, in professional services, or inside an embedded finance / fintech environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to Toast POS or other restaurant management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with AI tools (ie - Claude, GPT, Gemini, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A CPA, CB, or equivalent bookkeeping/accounting credential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
