&lt;p&gt;Toast creates technology to help restaurants and local businesses succeed in a digital world, helping business owners operate, increase sales, engage customers, and keep employees happy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Principal Software Engineer to join our data platform (AAP) team in Dublin. The AAP team owns the foundational data infrastructure that powers Toast&#39;s analytics products and AI/ML capabilities: real-time streaming pipelines, a cloud-native data lakehouse, feature serving for ML-driven product experiences, and the infrastructure that enables product teams across Toast to build intelligent, data-driven experiences for our 170,000+ restaurant customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are in the middle of a significant platform evolution: migrating to Apache Iceberg, standing up a new Feature Store, and scaling our streaming infrastructure to meet the demands of a rapidly growing business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Software Engineer, you&#39;ll contribute to the technical strategy for our most critical data platform initiatives - deep hands-on work with Spark and Iceberg, driving architectural decisions grounded in how these technologies actually behave under load, and helping shape the platform&#39;s touch points with the same care you&#39;d bring to an external product. You&#39;ll work closely with other senior engineers and technical leads, influence adjacent teams, and mentor engineers across the organisation - articulating technical direction clearly to engineering, product, and leadership, and bringing people along through a significant platform transformation. Success looks like other engineering teams moving faster because of the platform you help build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life (Responsibilities)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with Spark, Iceberg, and our streaming infrastructure - diagnosing performance, reasoning through architectural decisions, and building systems that other teams depend on at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical strategy for data platform initiatives alongside other senior engineers and technical leads, translating complex problems into clear direction and executable plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve the platform&#39;s API surfaces so that engineers across Toast can self-service - adoption and ease-of-use are part of the job&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence adjacent teams and align stakeholders across engineering, product, and leadership on architectural decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers on the team and raise the bar on engineering practices across the organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tooling as a genuine force multiplier in your day-to-day work and help the team do the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need to thrive (Requirements)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in software engineering with meaningful experience in data platform or distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in Apache Spark and Apache Iceberg, not just operational familiarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in streaming infrastructure (Apache Kafka, Apache Pulsar, or similar) and cloud-native data platforms on AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing internal platforms and developer-facing abstractions - you think about your platform&#39;s users as carefully as product engineers think about end users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive technical alignment across multi-team environments, including the communication work that makes architectural changes actually stick&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databricks experience is a bonus but we care more that you understand what&#39;s running underneath it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our tech stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our data platform runs on AWS and spans Apache Iceberg for table format and lakehouse architecture, Apache Kafka and Pulsar for real-time streaming, Apache Spark for data processing, and DynamoDB and Postgres for operational data stores. We are migrating from legacy ETL patterns toward a modern, cloud-native data lakehouse and building out Feature Store capabilities to power ML-driven product experiences. Our backend services are primarily Kotlin and Java.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**This is a hybrid role requiring in-office collaboration two days per week in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.toasttab.com/ireland&quot;&gt;Dublin office&lt;/a&gt;.**&lt;/p&gt;
