&lt;p&gt;As a Full-Stack Engineer you will have an opportunity to develop interactive web experiences and build and expand on the Toast Marketing web properties, focusing on our customer online learning experience.&amp;nbsp; The ideal candidate will “lean” to the front-end and possess strong communication in order to be able to effectively deliver on cross-team marketing initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life (Responsibilities)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While it is critically important to understand the “how” as a Full-Stack engineer on the marketing team, it is equally important to understand the “why” behind the projects you will be working on. You’re a perfect fit for this role if you are a detail-oriented problem solver, who can work and contribute to the marketing team not only as a developer, but as a resource to help provide feedback and insights into how we meet and exceed our team goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, test, and deliver clean, production-ready code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build fast, scalable websites and apps using React, Gatsby, and Tailwind CSS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build API integrations to fuel content production&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a clean and lightweight code repository for all production code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain front-end components using our internal design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure sites are accessible, performant, SEO/AEO-friendly, and responsive across all devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with project managers, web team members, and other Toast stakeholders as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape technical decisions, tooling, and best practices within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews and provide feedback to peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
