&lt;p&gt;Toast creates technology to help restaurants and local businesses succeed in a digital world, helping business owners operate, increase sales, engage customers, and keep employees happy. Over 180,000 restaurant businesses run on Toast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Senior Software Engineer to join our OLAP Platform team in Dublin. OLAP is the analytical data layer that powers real-time reporting, search and agentic data access for AI-driven products across Toast. We ingest events from across the business, index them into OpenSearch, and expose them to consumer teams through a federated GraphQL layer. One platform, many tenants, restaurant-critical latency and freshness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is in a pivotal stretch of work: scaling the platform to support more domains and more consumers, keeping performance and cost in balance as it grows, and opening it up safely to the next wave of AI-driven products. This is platform engineering at real scale - the systems you build here are consumed by other engineering teams and, downstream, by the tens of thousands of restaurants that run on Toast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need to thrive (Requirements)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong backend engineering skills in Kotlin, Java, or another object-oriented language, with solid instincts around testing and code quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large datasets, where correctness, freshness, and query performance all matter at the same time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with document-based or columnar data stores (BigTable, DynamoDB or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong interest in core search engineering e.g. ranking algorithms, semantic search, natural language search etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work across team boundaries and pick up context quickly - OLAP touches almost every product area at Toast, and the work can be as much collaboration as execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to break down a problem, understand what the consuming team actually needs, and ship a clean solution. Our users are other engineers, and the ergonomics of the platform matter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tooling as a genuine part of your workflow, not an afterthought&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will help you stand out (Nonessential Skills/Nice to Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing platform APIs that other teams depend on - platform thinking, not just feature delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with OpenSearch, Elasticsearch, or a similar query engine at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data pipelines or event-driven architectures (Kafka, Pulsar, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with federated GraphQL (ElasticGraph, Apollo Federation, or similar) and REST API design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Ruby, with the ability to navigate, understand, or modify existing source code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A core of Java &amp;amp; Kotlin based backend services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OpenSearch as the core query engine with ElasticGraph on top for federated GraphQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pulsar &amp;amp; Camel for message-based integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React SPAs leveraging Tailwind, GraphQL and Storybook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And many more technologies that help us build a top class platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**This is a hybrid role requiring in-office collaboration two days per week in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.toasttab.com/ireland&quot;&gt;Dublin office&lt;/a&gt;.**&lt;/p&gt;
